# Base URL of the NestJS backend API this frontend calls.
#
# Read server-side only: next.config.ts rewrites /api/* to it, and the Server
# Component in src/app/page.tsx fetches it directly. That is why it has NO
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and is never inlined into the browser bundle, and it is
# also why the app needs no CORS handling of its own - to the browser every call
# is same-origin.
#
# Never expose secrets via NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars; real secrets live in the team
# secret manager and, for Vercel, in the project's Environment Variables settings.
#
# DEPLOYED (RUN-60): set this in the host's env config to the backend's public
# origin, scheme + host, NO trailing slash and NO /api suffix (the rewrite adds
# the path), e.g.
#     BACKEND_URL=https://runlog-backend.onrender.com
# It must stay a plain server-side variable. Giving it a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix
# would bake the backend URL into every browser bundle permanently and hand the
# browser a cross-origin target, which is exactly what the rewrite avoids.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
